    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7938",
      "problem": "The graph below is a translation of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$ Find the equation that generated the graph.    \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/d7705be833455f266e892f78ec29f0dee88a7e3e803a00f85dfdfd15ff5f6f92.png)",
      "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the  left by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+2}.$\n\n- Translate the result  down by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+2}-1.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/9af181a909b6ed88cee9ab8d331a09378ed75cc85a33d0f156a5b89ac91796cf.png)\n\nTherefore, the answer is $y=\\sqrt{x+2}-1.$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/observations/step-e7938-527361e98374d624bf7a.html",
